  "body": "Use `SharedWorkerOptions` when a string is supplied as the second argument to `SharedWorker()`. This gives the legacy name overload the same `extendedLifetime: false` default as the dictionary overload, which the subsequent reuse check and initialization both read.\n\nThe existing [shared worker name test](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/e3baabe076221e80d9c07d9aea2cbefa7ad656b6/workers/shared-worker-name-via-options.html) exercises reusing a worker across the two overloads.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13248/workers.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 12, 2026, 10:58 AM UTC (f3d3edb)\">/workers.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/13248/91052e8...f3d3edb/workers.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 12, 2026, 10:58 AM UTC (f3d3edb)\">diff</a> )",
